  "updatedAt": "2026-07-27T11:40:15.467Z",
  "handoff": "# Session handoff — 2026-07-27\n\n> **Parked here, not about this phase.** F003/P017 (the phase this session worked) is **closed**, so\n> a handoff on it would never be opened. This is a session handoff, stored on the phase\n> `resume.json` calls current (F006/P005) so `/planner load` surfaces it. Nothing below is a\n> statement about F006/P005's own work.\n\n**Created at:** 2026-07-27\n**Updated at:** 2026-07-27\n**Reason:** Work finished and shipped for review. Not a context-exhaustion handoff — there is no\nhalf-done edit anywhere.\n\n## Current focus\n\n**Nothing is in progress. No task is started.** The branch is pushed and the PR is open:\n\n- **PR #249** — https://github.com/ovidius72/heca/pull/249 — branch `feat/action-arg-declaration`,\n  **20 commits**, 241 files, +6384/−1702. Awaiting review/merge.\n- **F003/P017 CLOSED** (all nine tasks). **F003/P010 CLOSED.** Both close with that PR.\n- Whole workspace green at every commit: **961 tests, 24 suites, clippy 0 warnings.**\n\n## What was being done\n\nF003/P017/T009 — \"move the view model to its own crate + make `realize` callable from below `heca`\"\n(Level 2, decided by the user 2026-07-26/27). Delivered in six commits:\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `a81f068` | **`heca-view`** — the model out of the app. `serde` only: no widget library, no renderer, no taffy. |\n| `f098e99` | `realize` takes **seams**: `IntentEmitter` = `Rc<dyn Fn(Intent)>`, plus the `HintTargets` trait. |\n| `8519db4` | **`heca-view-realize`** — the mapper below the app. |\n| `541c479` | The showcase renders a described tree beside its hand-built twin. |\n| `01f14c8` | `fix(row)`: an inset state highlight can no longer be shorter than its content. |\n| `d1eb204` | The demo rows get padding, like every other row on the page. |\n| `f9a11b1` | Planner state: T009 + phase closed, `resume.json` corrected. |\n\n**The user verified the showcase section in the running app and said \"looks good\".** That was T009's\nwhole acceptance — it is not a test-only claim.\n\n### The one non-obvious piece of design, so it is not undone by accident\n\n`HintTargetRegistry` **cannot** become `Intent`-keyed, although it looks like it should. The same\nregistry holds the modal action buttons' `InteractionIntent::ActivateAction(SubmitOverlay{..})`,\nwhich is not a view intent. So the registry still stores the app's carrier, and the seam is the one\noperation `realize` performs on it. `ViewHintTargets<'a>` in `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` is the only\nthing that knows both sides; `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs` (`build_modal_root`) is the **one**\nproduction caller and wraps both seams there.\n\n## How to resume\n\n1. `/planner load`, then **read the task before believing the recap** (see Reminder).\n2. Nothing to finish. Pick from Next steps, `planner-task-start` it, then work.\n3. If the PR comes back with review comments, they land on `feat/action-arg-declaration`, which is\n   pushed and tracking `origin`.\n\n## Files touched\n\nNew crates: `heca-view/{Cargo.toml,src/lib.rs}`, `heca-view-realize/{Cargo.toml,src/lib.rs}`.\nWorkspace members + `heca/Cargo.toml` + `heca-renderer/Cargo.toml` (both new crates are **dev**-deps\nof the renderer, for the showcase — that is not a cycle).\n`heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (re-exports + `ViewHintTargets`), `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs` (boundary\nwrapping). `heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs` (`Base::highlight_rect`),\n`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs` (`Layout::pad_left/pad_right/pad_top/pad_bottom`; `to_taffy` reads them),\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/{row.rs,item.rs}`, `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs` (the guard).\n`heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs` (`described_tree`, `native_twin`, `described_vs_native`,\n`ShowcaseHints`).\n\n## Blockers\n\n- **F003/P011/T012** (`126d0855`) is `blocked`, and the reason needs **re-checking, not planning\n  around**: \"no chrome surface mounts a ScrollRegion\" was verified 2026-07-17, and the 2026-07-26\n  sidebar scroll work may already have discharged it. Its horizontal trigger was settled 2026-07-27\n  as `prefix+Shift+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown` — the same four keys as vertical, Shift for the other\n  axis.\n- Nothing else. No failing test, no unverified visual, no half-applied edit.\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. **Merge PR #249** (or handle its review). Everything else is downstream of it.\n2. Unblocked by T009, neither started: **F003/P001/T006** (generate widget definitions for\n   JS/Python from `WidgetKind::ALL` — a closed list with a coverage guard already walking it) and\n   **F003/P011/T006** (the typed builder SDK can now genuinely re-export the model). Also check\n   whether F003/P017/T003's generated property tables are reusable outside the app; they are the\n   natural source for those definitions.\n3. Or the phase this handoff is parked on, **F006/P005 app-10 (Sidebar/chrome leftovers)**, which\n   has three planned tasks: T001 column-level pick keycaps, T004 sidebar drop loses panes, T005\n   sidebar cwd appears late.\n\n## Recent decisions\n\n- **Two crates, not one** (user, 2026-07-27): `heca-view` = model with `serde` only;\n  `heca-view-realize` = `realize` + `FormBindings` + tests, depending on `heca-view` and\n  `heca-grid-ui`. One crate would have dragged the widget library into every dependant of the model,\n  losing the reason a plugin can depend on it. **`heca-theme` turned out NOT to be needed** —\n  `Theme` is re-exported by `heca-grid-ui`.\n- **A fix goes in the widget.** The pill defect was fixed as `Base::highlight_rect`, which every\n  widget drawing an inset highlight now calls; `Item` had the identical arithmetic and the same\n  latent bug. The per-side padding cascade got one home so layout and paint cannot drift.\n- **Measure before believing a plan.** Two of T009's own measurements were wrong: **one** production\n  caller of `realize`, not two, and **four** import lines naming the module path, not eleven files.\n  Both corrected in the task. Likewise the second \"badge overflows\" report was the badge's *glow*\n  (`GLOW_RADIUS = 10.0`, painted outside its box by design — row 37px, badge box 35px centred), not\n  a layout fault; the demo rows were simply the only unpadded rows on the page.\n- **F003/P010/T005 stays CANCELED.** 148 names against 132 handler-bearing variants — they do not\n  pair 1:1, so the rewrite would have added code plus 148 hand-paired literals. Its safety is now\n  two guard tests. **Do not re-plan it.**\n\n## Reminder\n\n- **`.planner/HANDOFF.md` is DEPRECATED** — `planner-handoff-prepare` says so. Handoffs are\n  entity-scoped on `phase.handoff` now. The file in the repo was committed in `f9a11b1` for the\n  record only (it was recovered from the planner's `.bak` after being consumed, and had never been\n  committed). Do not write it again.\n- **`resume.json`'s `nextSteps`/`notes`/`lastSessionSummary` are free text that task operations do\n  NOT refresh, and they have misdirected two sessions now.** This one opened with a recap saying\n  \"T009 … do not start it\" when the user had already decided it and recorded the decision in the\n  task. **Read the task itself.** Correcting the file needs an authorized bypass, because the guard\n  blocks writes exactly when no task is in-progress — which is when it is wrong.\n- **`planner-task-show` and `planner-phase-update` can exceed the tool output limit** (T009's task\n  is ~119k chars). The response is saved to a file; read it with python/jq rather than retrying.\n  `planner-phase-update` **does** apply the change even when its response is too large to display —\n  check the file before assuming it failed. Phase `status` is **derived from the tasks**, so the\n  phase JSON keeps `status: null` while the tool correctly reports `done`.\n- **The user verifies rendering and interaction themselves.** Green tests are never verification for\n  anything visual — and if something cannot be seen in the app, say so plainly instead of offering a\n  look at something that should be identical. T009 existed largely to remove that excuse.\n- **Full planner ids, always** (`F003/P017/T009`), never `T9` or a slug. **Never decide whether a\n  task lives or dies** — bring the analysis and a recommendation. **A question in progress is not\n  permission to act.** **Never propose deferring work** to a later phase to avoid effort.\n- **`git checkout <file>` to undo an experiment wipes uncommitted work.** Copy to the scratchpad\n  first. (Also how a whole uncommitted handoff nearly died this session.)",
  "handoffUpdatedAt": "2026-07-27T13:37:24.584Z"
}